corn job overlap 
    Solution: Use flock in cron
    Suppose your backup script takes 15 minutes to finish, but cron runs it every 10 minutes.
    Without a lock, the second execution can start while the first is still running.
    Use:
    */10 * * * * /usr/bin/flock -n /tmp/backup.lock /bin/bash /opt/scripts/backup.sh >> /var/log/backup.log 2>&1
